# @olonjs/core Engine

## Fundamental constraint

Core must NOT contain tenant-specific logic (sections, schemas, data, theme choices). If a change requires knowledge of a specific section type or data shape, it belongs in the tenant, not core.

## Protocols

- **MTRP (Module Type Registry Protocol):** `contract/kernel.ts` defines the empty registries (`SectionDataRegistry`, `SectionSettingsRegistry`, `CollectionItemRegistry`), `BaseSection`, `Section` — tenants fill them via `declare module '@olonjs/core'` (module augmentation, never by editing core)
- **TBP (Tenant Block Protocol):** sections are capsules with `View.tsx`, `schema.ts`, `types.ts`, `index.ts` — capsule code lives in the tenant, core only provides the base schemas
- **JSP (JsonPages Site Protocol):** `src/data/config/{site,menu,theme}.json` + `src/data/pages/[slug].json` file ontology, consumed by the engine
- **COP (Collection Protocol):** collections resolved via `$ref` bindings — resolution logic in `contract/config-resolver.ts`

## Real file structure (post-ADR-0016 split — verified against source)

`src/` is organized by domain. Zero React at runtime (`import type React` only, in `contract/types-engine.ts`):

| Domain | Contents | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `contract/` | `kernel.ts` (MTRP registries, `Section`, `PageConfig`, `SiteConfig`, `ThemeConfig`, `MenuConfig`, `ProjectState`), `types-engine.ts` (`JsonPagesConfig`, `SelectionPath`, `PersistenceConfig`), `config-resolver.ts` ($ref resolution: JSON Pointer, aliases, circularity guard, `collection:current`, menu/collection draft bindings), `selection-path.ts`, `section-ops.ts`, `studio-events.ts` (`STUDIO_EVENTS`), `theme-logic.ts` (`buildThemeVariableMap`), `webmcp-contracts.ts` (page/manifest/collection contracts, `buildLlmsTxt`), `zod-schemas.ts` (internal SOT for the canonical JSON Schemas; `zod/v3` dialect) | Pure TS/Zod |
| `routing/` | `route-utils.ts` (slug normalization, `[param]` template matching), `public-page-document.ts` (`resolvePublicPageDocument`), `head-sync.ts` | Pure TS, DOM-guarded |
| `webmcp/` | `runtime/webmcp-bridge.ts` (`document.modelContext`, tool registry, `ensureWebMcpRuntime`, mutation helpers) | DOM-level, no React |
| `dna/` | `lib/base-schemas.ts` (BSDS: `ImageSelectionSchema`, `BaseSectionData`, `BaseArrayItem`, `BaseSectionSettingsSchema`, `CtaSchema`, `WithFormRecipient`), `lib/cloudSaveStream.ts`, `lib/deploySteps.ts`, `types/deploy.ts` | Pure TS/Zod |
| `assets/` | `asset-resolver.ts` (`resolveAssetUrl`, canonical URL validation) | Pure TS |
| `url/` | `base-path.ts` (`withBasePath`, `normalizeBasePath`) | Pure TS |
| `lib/` | `utils.ts` (`cn` = clsx + tailwind-merge — the only two runtime deps) | Pure TS |
| `kernel/` | Barrel re-export of `contract/kernel` | — |

Engine rendering (`JsonPagesEngine`, `PageRenderer`, `SectionRenderer`, theme runtime, `ConfigContext`) lives in **`@olonjs/react`**; editor UI (`FormFactory`, `StudioStage`, Inspector) lives in **`@olonjs/studio`**. Do not add React or editor code to this package — that reverses ADR-0016.

## Package shape (ADR-0016, implemented)

The former dual-bundle `/runtime` subpath (ADR-0009) is retired: `@olonjs/core` ships a single build (ESM + UMD), single `"."` export, `sideEffects: false` (ADR-0011). `vite.config.ts` externalizes only `zod` (peer `^4.6.0`); runtime deps are `clsx` and `tailwind-merge`.

Boundary enforcement: `npm run test:boundary` runs `scripts/check-package-boundaries.mjs` (repo root) — core must never import react/studio; studio never react; react → studio only via the single dynamic import in `packages/react/src/engine/StudioRoute.tsx`.

## Public API surface

All public exports go through `src/index.ts` (conceptual surfaces `contract`, `kernel`, `webmcp` + flat re-exports). When adding exports:
1. Keep the export framework-agnostic — no React, no DOM at import time
2. Verify it does not leak tenant-specific types
3. Consider backward compatibility — removing an export is a breaking change

## Compliance priority

1. Data is bound correctly
2. Schemas describe fields correctly
3. Content is editable without breaking the inspector
4. Tenant structure stays standardized
5. Context-aware focus/highlight is desirable but secondary
